{"ts":"2026-08-31T12:41:05.904Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"c41a528b9f424137989cc889","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"ops-3j1z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"Repair an incomplete release triple, instead of only reporting it every day"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"The release-completeness audit now runs unconditionally after Create GitHub release, so an incomplete predecessor is reported every day until it is repaired. Nothing repairs it. A run that publishes to npm and pushes its tag and then fails before creating the GitHub Release leaves a triple that no subsequent run completes, because the next run has no source changes and skips the release path entirely. That is exactly what happened here: v2026.08.28, v2026.08.29 and v2026.08.31 were published and tagged with no GitHub Release for fourteen days, and the three releases were created by hand on 2026-08-31, each body generated from its committed changelog section. The automation should do the same: for every release tag that has a published npm version and no GitHub Release, create the release from that version's changelog section. Held out of pull request 77 deliberately, because it is a write path into the releases API inside a job that already publishes to npm and pushes tags, and it deserves its own review rather than arriving inside a change about detection. Raised in review by Greptile as P1 and by CodeRabbit as a Major data-integrity finding."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Feature"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":[]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-31T12:41:05.904Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T12:41:05.904Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"claude-orchestrator"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"3b4787423a4c2b97209cf65ef167b526e835833fb82c3e0f102fafbb28fcd445","item_hash_version":2,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
{"ts":"2026-08-31T12:41:06.465Z","author":"claude-orchestrator","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"c41a528b9f424137989cc889","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"update","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-31T12:41:06.465Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"For each release tag with a published npm version and no GitHub Release, the release job creates the missing GitHub Release from that version's committed changelog section; the step is idempotent, so a run with nothing to repair makes no API writes; a tag with no published npm version is never given a GitHub Release, since that would assert a release that was never published; the repair is covered by hermetic tests with an injected client and no network"}],"before_hash":"3b4787423a4c2b97209cf65ef167b526e835833fb82c3e0f102fafbb28fcd445","after_hash":"487bae5f255c2b76a0164f92bac615a130df37bc88146f2bdacee974f3ff09fc","item_hash_version":2,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"failed","reason":"resolver_failed","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}}}
